// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 22-surface-syntax
// facility: spec/22 §1 byte-char-literal (lexical ill-formedness); D-0033
// kind: negative
// expect: parse-error
//
// A `byte-char-literal` holds exactly one byte: `b'ab'` is lexically
// ill-formed. Several bytes are a `byte-literal`, `b"ab"`.

fn main()
{
    u8 c = b'ab';
}
